e same window includes idempotency keys and did not duplicate.\n\n## Highest-Confidence Follow-Up Action\n\nReject bulk-refund requests unless they include an idempotency key; remove the `legacy_batch_header` bypass before re-enabling the endpoint.\n\n## Unresolved Ambiguity\n\nWorker replay was an early symptom theory but is not supported as the primary trigger by final evidence.\n=== findings.json ===\n{\n  \"ranked_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"bulk-refund requests accepted without idempotency keys\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"corpus/timeline/incident_timeline.md: 10:17 UTC bulk refund requests accepted without idempotency keys\", \"corpus/tickets/TICKET-8729.md: every duplicate has request_class=bulk-refund and no idempotency key\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"idempotency-required guardrail skipped due to legacy_batch_header\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"corpus/timeline/incident_timeline.md: 10:18 UTC idempotency-required guardrail skipped due to legacy_batch_header\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"reject bulk-refund requests without idempotency keys and remove legacy_batch_header bypass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"corpus/remediation/notes.md: bulk-refund requests must be rejected unless they include an idempotency key; remove the legacy_batch_header bypass before re-enabling the endpoint\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolved_ambiguity\": \"worker replay was an early symptom theory but is not supported as the primary trigger by final evidence\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
